 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34S 2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34S  c  1968Mo22: {+34}S(p,p') with a 12.011-MeV {I17} proton beam from the    
 34S 2c  ONR-CIT tandem accelerator on a CdS target 85%-enriched in {+34}S. The 
 34S 3c  scattered protons were detected using an array of 16 Au-Si surface     
 34S 4c  barrier detectors with FWHM=25 keV at the focal plane of a double      
 34S 5c  focusing magnetic spectrometer. Measured |s(E{-p}). Deduced levels.    

 34S  c  1991Ke09, 1991Kh06: {+34}S(pol p,p') with a 318-MeV polarized proton   
 34S 2c  beam on a target 67.92%-enriched in {+34}S (powder in between thin     
 34S 3c  beryllium foils). Scattered protons were analyzed using the            
 34S 4c  high-resolution spectrometer at the Los Alamos Meson Physics Facility  
 34S 5c  at angles between 5|' and 39|'. Measured differential cross sections   
 34S 6c  and analyzing powers.                                                  
 34S  c  1985Al03: {+34}S(p,p') with a 29.8-MeV proton beam on a target         
 34S 2c  94.3%-enriched in {+34}S on C backing. Scattered protons were detected 
 34S 3c  using a position-sensitive gas proportional counter (FWHM=20 keV).     
 34S 4c  Measured angular distributions covering the angles from 15|' to 120|'  
 34S 5c  in steps of 5|'.                                                       
 34S  c  1983Iv01: {+34}S(p,p') with a 6-MeV proton beam. Measured elastic and  
 34S 2c  inelastic angular distributions.                                       
 34S  c  1975Al28: {+34}S(p,p') with a 1-GeV proton beam on a target            
 34S 2c  98.0%-enriched in {+34}S. Scattered protons were detected using a      
 34S 3c  magnetic spectrometer (quadrupole lens doublet, magnet, detecting      
 34S 4c  system of scintillator counters). Measured elastic and inelastic       
 34S 5c  differential cross sections.                                           
 34S  c  1975Al08: {+34}S(p,p') with a 1-GeV proton beam, using the same type of
 34S 2c  target and the same experimental setup as those in 1975Al28 (FWHM=1.6  
 34S 3c  MeV). Measured elastic differential cross sections.                    
 34S  c  1974Gu26: {+34}S(p,p') with 5.4-6.2-MeV proton beams on a thick target 
 34S 2c  97.97%-enriched in {+34}S (sulfur on glass plate). Measured excitation 
 34S 3c  functions at several angles and elastic angular distributions.         
 34S  c  1973Go42: {+34}S(pol p,p') with a 24.5-MeV polarized proton beam.      
 34S 2c  Measured differential cross sections and asymmetries (as function of   
 34S 3c  angle) for inelastic proton scattering.                                

 34S 2c  1972Pl06: {+34}S(pol p,p') with a 24.5-MeV polarized proton beam. 
 34S  c  1969An35: {+34}S(p,p') with a 6.03-MeV proton beam on an InS target    
 34S 2c  57.17%-enriched in {+34}S. Scattered protons were detected using a     
 34S 3c  Si(Li) detector. Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced levels, J, and |p.     

 34S  c  1985SaZS: {+34}S(pol p,p') with a 65-MeV polarized proton beam.        
 34S 2c  Scattered protons were analyzed using a high-resolution magnetic       
 34S 3c  spectrograph. Measured angular distributions of the differential cross 
 34S 4c  sections and analyzing powers for a number of states.                  
 34S  c  1978BeXU: {+34}S(p,p') with a 40-MeV proton beam on a thick            
 34S 2c  sandwich-type target. Scattered protons were detected using an Enge    
 34S 3c  split-pole spectrometer and position-sensitive proportional counter    
 34S 4c  backed with plastic scintillator (additional runs on photographic      
 34S 5c  plates too).                                                           
